# Patch:        010-skip-wasm-demo-binaries
# Phase:        pre
# Target:       goldilocks/Cargo.toml
# Hunks:        1
# Class:        bound
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 1 (hax passes no target selection to
#               charon, so its cargo build also compiles the binaries).
#               Without this patch the cargo check of the extracted variant
#               fails on the binaries: "can't find crate for `std`" (E0463).
# Cost:         none. The library is untouched; the two demo binaries are not built.
# Upstreamable: no: the binaries are wanted upstream. A hax option forwarding
#               `--lib` to charon would make the patch unnecessary.
# Drop when:    hax forwards cargo target selection to charon, or the binaries
#               leave src/bin.
# Test:         test p3-goldilocks --lib
# Mutation:     the manifest also drops the library, so the library tests are gone.
#
# p3-goldilocks has two auto-discovered wasm32 demo binaries in src/bin.
#
# Both need std, which thumbv7em-none-eabi lacks.
#
# Charon's cargo build compiles them, fails, and never reaches the library.
#
# hax appends its own `--` to the charon command, so `--lib` cannot be passed.
#
# `autobins = false` stops cargo from discovering the binaries.
#
# The library and its tests build exactly as shipped.
#
# Tested:     test-pre-patches.py: 6715 of 6769 upstream tests pass as
#             shipped, 6715 with the pre-patches; 0 divergences from this patch.
#
diff --git a/goldilocks/Cargo.toml b/goldilocks/Cargo.toml
index f2b8b02d..ed1de255 100644
--- a/goldilocks/Cargo.toml
+++ b/goldilocks/Cargo.toml
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@ repository.workspace = true
 homepage.workspace = true
 keywords.workspace = true
 categories.workspace = true
+# PATCHED: the wasm32 demo binaries in src/bin need std, which the extraction target lacks.
+autobins = false
 
 # criterion pulls rayon transitively and rayon does not build on wasi.
 [target.'cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))'.dev-dependencies]
